Am Sam Ath, senior technical supervisor at Licadho, said the rights group was aware of the arrests. “If they just planned to hold a protest outside the Vietnamese Embassy, then they should not have been arrested,” he said.
The statement also accuses Mr. Serey of plotting terrorist activities, including the placement of explosives in front of the Council of Ministers and TV3 station in Phnom Penh in 2009. The government previously blamed another supposed terrorist organization, the Tiger Head Movement, of planting the explosives, which never went off.
