Difference in plasticization: UPVC is rigid PVC, a modified material is prepared by adding a certain amount of modification additives on the basis of PVC resin powder. Therefore, the main difference between UPVC and PVC and soft PVC is that no plasticizer is added, there are more calcium powders, and the material has high mechanical strength.
Difference in chlorine content: CPVC is chlorinated polyvinyl chloride, which increases the chlorine content in PVC materials through a certain process on the basis of PVC resin, thereby improving the heat resistance, acid, alkali, salt, and oxidant of the material. The corrosion of the material increases the thermal deformation temperature and mechanical properties of the material.
Differences in use: UPVC is suitable for producing valve pipes, etc. CPVC is mainly used in fire-fighting pipes, chemical corrosion-resistant pipes and civil hot water pipes.
Precautions when injection molding PVC:
The product should not have sharp corners or sudden changes as much as possible, and the thickness should not change much to prevent the degradation of PVC.
The mold temperature should have a cooling water control device, so that the mold temperature can be controlled between 30°C and 60°C.
It is necessary to avoid other plastic PVC raw materials, which will cause the deterioration of PVC raw materials. Especially when other raw materials have been injected, the plastic in the barrel and screw must be cleaned before injection of PVC products.
