To prevent oxidation, some modified plastics require the addition of large amounts of antioxidants, which may seep into the water supply and cause unpleasant odors.
The oxygen limit index of CPVC (Chlorinated polyvinyl Chloride) is 60℃, so it will not burn in the air. With no flame dripping, no increase in fire load, limited flame spread, low smoke generation characteristics.
No thermally dependent material has shown its superior properties as CPVC (Chlorinated polyvinyl Chloride), which has survived four decades of maintenance-free hot water systems.
